  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the most probable outcome (i.e., the outcome with the highest individual probability) in each lottery. In both lotteries, this is 0 Euros (67% for A, 66% for B). The reason would prefer Lottery A because its most probable outcome has a higher probability, even though both outcomes are identical (0 Euros). However, the individual in the verbal report focuses on the chance of winning (i.e., the probability of a positive outcome), which is 33% vs. 34%. This reflects attention to the less probable but favorable outcome, not the most probable one. The individual is drawn to the 1% increase in the chance of winning, which aligns with comparing the probabilities of the best outcomes, not the most probable ones. Therefore, the information considered by the individual (probability of non-zero gain) differs from that required by the decision reason (probability and value of the single most likely outcome). Furthermore, the justification is based on increased winning chances, not on dominance in the most probable outcome. There is no indication that the individual considered 0 Euros as the key point of comparison or that they preferred a lottery because its most likely result was more probable. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
